      "name": null,
      "problem": "Factor the expression ${h}^{7}+8{h}^{6}+16{h}^{5}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that all of the terms have a common factor of ${h}^{5}.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the ${h}^{5},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{7}+8{h}^{6}+16{h}^{5} & ={h}^{5}({h}^{2}+8h+16)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe expression ${h}^{2}+8h+16$ is a perfect square trinomial that can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{5}({h}^{2}+8h+16) & = \\\\ {h}^{5}({h}^{2}+8h+{4}^{2}) & = \\\\ {h}^{5}({h}^{2}+2\\cdot 4h+{4}^{2}) & = \\\\ {h}^{5}(h+4)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
